  "conclusions": [
    "First four IRQ30 slots alternate high A/B, all masks 7 including ready low; high A and B then block, selecting low. No lower-class guarantee under permanent high saturation.",
    "Yielding worker consumes one unit twice on early SVCs, leaves 2 then 1; third unit via IRQ demotes to level 1 with 4 units behind waiting CPU. CPU subsequently consumes 4, goes to level 0. At service 12 worker blocks, interactive wakes (mask 6 to 5), boost restores all ranks and budgets, picks previously eligible CPU then interactive resumes its original SVC continuation.",
    "17 incoming ERETs and ELRs match ELF task entries or private saved continuations; 8 IRQ30s, 9 SVCs; stable distinct frames per phase/task. Final phase row has empty ready set; no dispatch PC.",
    "Whole counter intervals from dispatch to trap capped by grant, flooring fractions; post-stop to subsequent dispatch excluded; interval can include trap-entry/dispatch overhead. 25 units/second by specification; single emulated run measures event order and counter intervals, no hardware, fairness beyond observed trace, deadline guarantee or target performance certification. Host invalid/repeated-stop cases are outside this single boot."
  ]
